{"id":"reverse_cable_crossover","name":"Reverse cable crossover","cue":"Arms soft, sweep wide and back, squeeze your shoulder blades.","research":"Standing reverse cable crossover (reverse cable fly), between two high pulleys (1.12 H, 2.0 m) 0.5 H (0.9 m) either side of the stance and 0.5 H (0.9 m) in front of it, each cable held in the OPPOSITE hand so the cables cross in front of the lifter, feet hip width, knees soft (6), trunk upright and still. Design values from the standard technique description, not a measured trial: the arms start forward just below shoulder height with the hands almost together in front of the chest (shoulder elevation 79, plane 96 across the midline, elbow 15, hands 0.82 H high and 0.07 H either side of the midline, shoulder blades spread: clavicle pro +10) and sweep wide and back to the line of the shoulders (elevation 88, plane -9 just behind the frontal plane, elbow 15, hands 0.46 H out, shoulder blades drawn back: clavicle pro -10), the elbows held at the same soft bend throughout. Stirrup handles ride on the fists (a free-swinging triangle on the grip bar that follows the cable, dswing). The two cables cross in front of the head and chest (closest 0.17 H to the head). Cable 1:1 to the stack, 0.48 H of travel. Geometry: design/cableA/rev.mjs.","targets":{"tol":10,"A":{"trunk_flexion":0,"shoulder_elevation":79,"shoulder_plane":96,"elbow_flexion":15,"knee_flexion":6},"B":{"trunk_flexion":0,"shoulder_elevation":88,"shoulder_plane":-9,"elbow_flexion":15},"note":"design values (standard technique), not a measured trial; the plane read-back is thorax-relative"},"muscles":{"primary":["delt_post","upper_back"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":165,"el":18,"dAz":0,"dEl":0,"fill":0.62,"note":"View from behind and a little to the right, raised (az 165, el 18, 20 deg off the view from behind): the rear shoulders and the upper back face the camera and the arms opening wide read as a T; the columns stand beyond the figure and the crossed